    Replace fake GCash QR with real uploaded QR; defuse dead Send Message buttons
    
    The POS "scan to pay" QR was a Material icon glyph with a made-up merchant
    ID — never a real, scannable code. Tried a generated QR encoding the
    account details as text, but confirmed on-device that the real GCash app
    rejects anything that isn't its own Personal/Merchant/Bank QR format. Since
    no legitimate GCash Merchant QR is reachable without formal business
    registration, the fix is to let the owner upload a photo of their own
    GCash app's Personal "My QR" code instead — a real, GCash-issued QR that
    actually works when scanned. Adds settings/gcash_account (accountName,
    accountNumber, qrImageUrl) with a new owner editor screen (Profile >
    Station Operations > Edit GCash Account), wired live into both the POS
    counter screen and the customer checkout screen; falls back to a plain
    "no QR uploaded yet" state rather than a fake placeholder. Account
    name/number are also now editable rather than hardcoded, so a maxed-out
    GCash number can be swapped without a code change.
    
    Also stops the two dead "Send Message" buttons (customer map screen,
    rider delivery queue) from silently doing nothing on tap — they now show
    a clear "coming soon" message instead.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

